      "settlement": "Vaelyssa",
      "settlementKey": "ceulrithan:Vaelyssa",
      "description": "Mara Murmury is an elderly Taudinax Dragonborn seer whose visions come through diluted ichor, pain, and the stubborn refusal to die before saying one more useful thing. People dismiss her as an addict until her warnings save a convoy, reveal a raider route, or name a child no one admitted was missing. The Freeblade Veil protect her because Mara's sight is dangerous, unreliable, and sometimes the only thing standing between refugees and a massacre.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Vaelyssa is a Village in Ceulrithan, under Confessional State, with low danger, Partial forest, Farming, Deep forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Taudinax Dragonborn reads through the Dragonborn entry of the race compendium, within Draconic and Reptilian Races, marked by Valkhamesh. Dragonborn are draconic humanoids born of ancient dragon lineage, elemental force, dynastic memory, and divine sovereignty. In Belavadös, a Dragonborn may carry traditional chromatic, metallic, or gem ancestry while a. Table cues: Dragon Ancestry, Breath Weapon, Damage Resistance, Darkvision; starting tendency Altruistic - Lawful - Cooperative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Mara can name the color of a disaster before anyone knows what burned.",
        "She swears every bottle of ichor-sight takes a tooth from the future."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Mara sends the party to a harmless-looking bridge hours before a refugee column is due to cross it.",
        "A healer offers to break Mara's ichor dependence, but her next vision says the cure will blind more than her."
      ],
